<title>UK: Clarke says to cut oil well coporation tax relief.</title>
<headline>Clarke says to cut oil well coporation tax relief.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday he proposed to withdraw the 100 percent corporation tax deduction for the intangible costs of drilling most production oil wells.</p>
<p>In his budget presentation, Clarke said these would be replaced by 25 percent capital allowances.</p>
<p>He also said that tax treatment of long-life assets would be brought more into line with accounting treatment. Capital allowance for plant and machinery with a life of more than 25 years would be cut to six percent on a reducing balance basis.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 2274</p>
